ChangeLog:
2026-10-18 bmcleodcd
    - Add Ortek VRC-1100 IR keyboard and mouse support through the built-in
      LCD receiver, including configurable mappings, learning/capture tools,
      repeat handling, acceleration, dragging and USB receiver suppression.
    - Add HP RC6 MCE and original Xbox DVD remote decoding and Kodi mappings,
      with timing validation, repeat suppression and captured-signal tests.
    - Replace X11/libxdo input with native Linux uinput keyboard and mouse
      devices; preserve shared key/button ownership and release held input
      on shutdown, launch, receiver takeover and input failures.
    - Isolate optional XRandR display sampling in a supervised helper so
      input and the main panel process operate independently of X11.
    - Complete live display diagnostics and panel service recovery setup.
    - Extend sanitizer/regression checks for input, remote decoders, display
      handling and captured keyboard/mouse signals; add live uinput checks.
    - Consolidate build, architecture, configuration, installation, rollback
      and EEPROM guidance in AGENTS.md; refresh README and legacy SDK notes.
    - Make documentation, map/capture filenames and learning output generic
      across machines; remove the unused bundled libxdo header.

2026-10-10 bmcleodcd
    - Show temporary display resolution/refresh-rate overlays, retaining the
      last mode across abrupt panel restarts and prioritizing volume overlays.

2026-10-09 bmcleodcd
    - Show CPU usage when NVML GPU temperature is unavailable, with bounded
      sensor sampling and placeholders for failed or initial readings.

2026-09-28 bmcleodcd
    - Refactor the Linux 20x2 panel loop; correct USB event/timeout handling,
      button press/release tracking, RC5 decoding and orderly shutdown.
    - Replace shell-based panel operations with native APIs, including
      asynchronous system D-Bus requests to start RetroArch.
    - Add background Kodi JSON-RPC and RetroArch UDP metadata sampling with
      timeouts; scroll media/game titles and retain titles while paused.
    - Add playback progress, pause/live status, volume/mute overlays and
      centred status messages, updating LCD rows only when content changes.
    - Add bounded EEPROM splash programming with acknowledgements, read-back
      verification, full backup/restore and rollback on failure; supply an
      animated cat power-on splash and checked installer.
    - Add private builds, sanitizer/regression checks and versioned panel
      installation with release checksums, service checks and rollback.

2023-08-10 bmcleodcd
    - Add NVIDIA GPU temperature reporting through NVML.

2023-07-19 to 2023-07-21 bmcleodcd
    - Add physical panel button actions and configurable key bindings using
      lookup tables; switch key injection from shell commands to libxdo
      (superseded by native Linux uinput in 2026).
    - Keep the panel clock updating between USB read-event timeouts and
      add CPU temperature reporting.

2010-03-12 Nicu Pavel (npavel@ituner.com)
    - 0.1.9 - release 
	- added support for picolcd 20x4 and 256x64 products
	- link with libusb-legacy on MacOS
	- use glibtoolize for MacOS
	- remove all calls to self->hid->interrupt_write with picolcd_send
	- silence all warnings
	- reduce the verbosity while compiling
	- added a _hid_unimplemented and _picolcd_unimplemented to tag 
	  the functions not implemented in usblcd operations struct
	- renamed driver vars 
	- make drivers filename nicer
	- fallback with return instead of exit
	- added support for 20x4 settext function
	- added a new function picolcd_send to easier send data to lcd
	- some spelling mistakes fixed
	- added picolcd-common.h
	- updated and fixed examples
	- changed header files from usblcd to picolcd
	- renamed main binary to picolcd
	- build system cleanup
	- move to picoLCD/libpicoLCD
	- code cleanups
